Below is a step‐by‐step decomposition of the mission description into a goal model for a multi‐robot system. The model is organized hierarchically using AND (sequential) and Fallback decompositions. In the collection phase a fallback is activated if the robot’s battery drops below 10%, while in the delivery phase a fallback is triggered if the battery falls below 30% (with an additional alert/report step if the fallback fails). Multiple robots may run their collection/delivery tasks in parallel when more than one storage item is required. 

